,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,4340,1657,5109,504,220,16,1526,220,17,15,15,614,264,220,17,304,279,8153,1992,323,525,74916,553,220,19,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many numbers from 1 through 200 have a 2 in the units place and are divisible by 4?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"10be6fe06c93b2b4fe606d08d498acd069f137d8410d9974868c7cf51e4ecec3"},"seconds":22.375715732574463,"seed":595180182977431934,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine how many numbers from 1 through 200 have a 2 in the units place and are divisible by 4, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the numbers with a 2 in the units place:**\n   These numbers are: 2, 12, 22, 32, 42, 52, 62, 72, 82, 92, 102, 112, 122, 132, 142, 152, 162, 172, 182, 192. These numbers form an arithmetic sequence with the first term 2 and a common difference of 10.\n\n2. **Check which of these numbers are divisible by 4:**\n   A number is divisible by 4 if its last two digits form a number that is divisible by 4. Therefore, we need to check the divisibility of the numbers 2, 12, 22, 32, 42, 52, 62, 72, 82, 92, 102, 112, 122, 132, 142, 152, 162, 172, 182, 192 by 4.\n   - 2 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 12 (divisible by 4)\n   - 22 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 32 (divisible by 4)\n   - 42 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 52 (divisible by 4)\n   - 62 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 72 (divisible by 4)\n   - 82 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 92 (divisible by 4)\n   - 102 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 112 (divisible by 4)\n   - 122 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 132 (divisible by 4)\n   - 142 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 152 (divisible by 4)\n   - 162 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 172 (divisible by 4)\n   - 182 (not divisible by 4)\n   - 192 (divisible by 4)\n\n   The numbers that are divisible by 4 are: 12, 32, 52, 72, 92, 112, 132, 152, 172, 192. These numbers form an arithmetic sequence with the first term 12 and a common difference of 20.\n\n3. **Count the number of terms in this sequence:**\n   The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by \\(a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\\), where \\(a_1\\) is the first term, \\(d\\) is the common difference, and \\(n\\) is the number of terms.\n   Here, \\(a_1 = 12\\), \\(d = 20\\), and the last term \\(a_n = 192\\).\n   \\[\n   192 = 12 + (n-1) \\cdot 20\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   192 = 12 + 20n - 20\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   192 = 20n - 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   200 = 20n\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{200}{20} = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of numbers from 1 through 200 that have a 2 in the units place and are divisible by 4 is \\(\\boxed{10}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{10}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:727"}
